From: VyOS SRX kernel build
Subject: builddeb: skip host-tool rebuild in headers deb for cross builds

scripts/package/install-extmod-build rebuilds the host programs (fixdep,
modpost, ...) inside the staged headers package with HOSTCC="${CC}", where
CC is the cross compiler when CROSS_COMPILE is set. That requires the
target libc on the build host, which the srx-kbuild image does not carry,
so bindeb-pkg fails at the binary-headers stage (sys/types.h not found).
Skip the rebuild for cross builds; the headers deb then ships the
host-built script binaries.

---
 scripts/package/install-extmod-build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/package/install-extmod-build b/scripts/package/install-extmod-build
--- a/scripts/package/install-extmod-build
+++ b/scripts/package/install-extmod-build
@@ -51,8 +51,8 @@
 # When ${CC} and ${HOSTCC} differ, rebuild host programs using ${CC}.
 #
 # This caters to host programs that participate in Kbuild. objtool and
 # resolve_btfids are out of scope.
-if [ "${CC}" != "${HOSTCC}" ]; then
+if [ "${CC}" != "${HOSTCC}" ] && [ -z "${CROSS_COMPILE}" ]; then
 	cat "${destdir}/scripts/Makefile" - <<-'EOF' > "${destdir}/scripts/Kbuild"
 	subdir-y += basic
 	hostprogs-always-y += mod/modpost
--
2.39.5

